r as a thoughtful, no-fuss Raya hamper.”\"}, {\"data\": {\"chunks\": [\"products.md#4-b9423d548dbcfac4\", \"brand.md#1-9eae976fa1da0c9c\", \"campaigns.md#3-b2c3e00cda085e89\", \"products.md#2-1fd832e6cfacf871\", \"products.md#0-9acf1c4f15ecbab2\", \"brand.md#2-0304363243e2d334\", \"campaigns.md#2-7dbaaede50334936\", \"brand.md#3-b27c3b7212dcf820\"]}, \"agent\": \"system\", \"phase\": \"finished\", \"detail\": \"Retrieved 8 brand chunks as ground truth\"}, {\"data\": {\"axes\": [\"hook\", \"setting\"], \"revising\": false}, \"agent\": \"copywriter\", \"phase\": \"started\", \"detail\": \"Writing 2 variants, one per axis\"}, {\"data\": {\"headlines\": [\"Raya gift, sorted.\", \"Office hamper, done.\"]}, \"agent\": \"copywriter\", \"phase\": \"finished\", \"detail\": \"2 variants written\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"agent\": \"visual_planner\", \"phase\": \"started\", \"detail\": \"Planning 2 images around the finished copy\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"agent\": \"visual_planner\", \"phase\": \"finished\", \"detail\": \"2 image briefs planned\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"agent\": \"director\", \"phase\": \"started\", \"detail\": \"Reviewing 2 pairs on brand, diversity, execution\"}, {\"data\": {\"notes\": \"Variant 1 (hook): The copy is fine, but the image brief contradicts the copy\'s need for negative space. The prompt specifies \'negative space in the top-right quadrant is intentionally kept minimal and uncluttered\', but then describes a \'centered\' composition with products \'slightly angled toward the camera\' and a \'softly blurred\' background with bokeh. This creates a visual conflict — if the products are centered and the background is blurred, there is no clean zone for the headline and CTA in the top-right. The prompt must describe a composition where the products are placed off-center (e.g., bottom-left or center-left) to genuinely leave the top-right clear for text. Variant 2 (setting): The copy is fine, but the image brief is weak on the \'setting\' axis. The prompt describes a \'modern, minimalist office desk scene\' with \'subtle office essentials\', but the composition is \'slightly off-center\' with products \'positioned toward the right side of the frame\'. This does not strongly differentiate it from Variant 1\'s flat-lay. To truly vary the setting, the image should show a more distinct office environment — e.g., a cubicle desk with a laptop, coffee cup, or office chair in the background — to make the \'office hamper\' context visually obvious and distinct from the cozy flat-lay of Variant 1.\", \"verdict\": \"revise_copy\"}, \"agent\": \"director\", \"phase\": \"failed\", \"detail\": \"Verdict: revise_copy — Variant 1 (hook): The copy is fine, but the image brief contradicts the copy\'s need for negative space. The prompt specifies \'negative space in the top-right quadrant is intentionally kept minimal and uncluttered\', but then describes a \'centered\' composition with products \'slightly angled toward the camera\' and a \'softly blurred\' background with bokeh. This creates a visual conflict — if the products are centered and the background is blurred, there is no clean zone for the headline and CTA in the top-right. The prompt must describe a composition where the products are placed off-center (e.g., bottom-left or center-left) to genuinely leave the top-right clear for text. Variant 2 (setting): The copy is fine, but the image brief is weak on the \'setting\' axis. The prompt describes a \'modern, minimalist office desk scene\' with \'subtle office essentials\', but the composition is \'slightly off-center\' with products \'positioned toward the right side of the frame\'. This does not strongly differentiate it from Variant 1\'s flat-lay. To truly vary the setting, the image should show a more distinct office environment — e.g., a cubicle desk with a laptop, coffee cup, or office chair in the background — to make the \'office hamper\' context visually obvious and distinct from the cozy flat-lay of Variant 1.\"}, {\"data\": {\"target\": \"copywriter\", \"revision\": 1}, \"agent\": \"system\", \"phase\": \"started\", \"detail\": \"Revision 1 of 2 → copywriter\"}, {\"data\": {\"axes\": [\"hook\", \"setting\"], \"revising\": true}, \"agent\": \"copywriter\", \"phase\": \"started\", \"detail\": \"Rewriting 2 variants, one per axis\"}, {\"data\": {\"headlines\": [\"Raya Gift, Sorted.\", \"From Desk to Duit Raya.\"]}, \"agent\": \"copywriter\", \"phase\": \"finished\", \"detail\": \"2 variants written\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"agent\": \"visual_planner\", \"phase\": \"started\", \"detail\": \"Planning 2 images around the finished copy\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"agent\": \"visual_planner\", \"phase\": \"finished\", \"detail\": \"2 image briefs planned\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"agent\": \"director\", \"phase\": \"started\", \"detail\": \"Reviewing 2 pairs on brand, diversity, execution\"}, {\"data\": {\"notes\": \"The set fails on both the BRAND and DIVERSITY tests.\\n\\n**BRAND:**\\nBoth variants misrepresent the sampling sachet offer. The copy states you must \\\"Add a few more items to hit RM120\\\" (V1) and \\\"Spend above RM120\\\" (V2). The company knowledge states the starter set is RM99 and \\\"Sampling sachets are attached free to any order above RM120.\\\" The copy implies the customer needs to buy additional items to reach the threshold, but the knowledge does not specify what those items are or if the RM99 starter set qualifies. This is a factual claim the company knowledge does not support.\\n\\n**DIVERSITY:**\\nThe assigned axes were \\\"hook\\\" (V1) and \\\"setting\\\" (V2). However, both variants use nearly identical hooks and settings:\\n- V1 hook: \\\"Raya Gift, Sorted.\\\" — a generic, benefit-driven hook.\\n- V2 hook: \\\"From Desk to Duit Raya.\\\" — also a generic, benefit-driven hook about gifting.\\n- V1 setting: A flat-lay gift arrangement on linen cloth (a product-focused, lifestyle setting).\\n- V2 setting: An office desk scene (also a product-focused, lifestyle setting).\\n\\nThe two variants are not meaningfully different along their assigned axes. The hooks are both generic gift-giving messages, and the settings are both lifestyle/product shots. They could stand in for each other. The copywriter must rewrite to create real variation: for example, a hook that leads with a specific product benefit or a question, and a setting that is genuinely distinct (e.g., a person using the product, a close-up texture shot, or a different environment entirely). The visuals will need replanning around the new copy.\", \"verdict\": \"revise_copy\"}, \"agent\": \"director\", \"phase\": \"failed\", \"detail\": \"Verdict: revise_copy — The set fails on both the BRAND and DIVERSITY tests.\\n\\n**BRAND:**\\nBoth variants misrepresent the sampling sachet offer. The copy states you must \\\"Add a few more items to hit RM120\\\" (V1) and \\\"Spend above RM120\\\" (V2). The company knowledge states the starter set is RM99 and \\\"Sampling sachets are attached free to any order above RM120.\\\" The copy implies the customer needs to buy additional items to reach the threshold, but the knowledge does not specify what those items are or if the RM99 starter set qualifies. This is a factual claim the company knowledge does not support.\\n\\n**DIVERSITY:**\\nThe assigned axes were \\\"hook\\\" (V1) and \\\"setting\\\" (V2). However, both variants use nearly identical hooks and settings:\\n- V1 hook: \\\"Raya Gift, Sorted.\\\" — a generic, benefit-driven hook.\\n- V2 hook: \\\"From Desk to Duit Raya.\\\" — also a generic, benefit-driven hook about gifting.\\n- V1 setting: A flat-lay gift arrangement on linen cloth (a product-focused, lifestyle setting).\\n- V2 setting: An office desk scene (also a product-focused, lifestyle setting).\\n\\nThe two variants are not meaningfully different along their assigned axes. The hooks are both generic gift-giving messages, and the settings are both lifestyle/product shots. They could stand in for each other. The copywriter must rewrite to create real variation: for example, a hook that leads with a specific product benefit or a question, and a setting that is genuinely distinct (e.g., a person using the product, a close-up texture shot, or a different environment entirely). The visuals will need replanning around the new copy.\"}, {\"data\": {\"target\": \"copywriter\", \"revision\": 2}, \"agent\": \"system\", \"phase\": \"started\", \"detail\": \"Revision 2 of 2 → copywriter\"}, {\"data\": {\"axes\": [\"hook\", \"setting\"], \"revising\": true}, \"agent\": \"copywriter\", \"phase\": \"started\", \"detail\": \"Rewriting 2 variants, one per axis\"}, {\"data\": {\"headlines\": [\"Kulit Berminyak? This Raya Gift Works.\", \"Open the Drawer. Find the Gift.\"]}, \"agent\": \"copywriter\", \"phase\": \"finished\", \"detail\": \"2 variants written\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"agent\": \"visual_planner\", \"phase\": \"started\", \"detail\": \"Planning 2 images around the finished copy\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"agent\": \"visual_planner\", \"phase\": \"finished\", \"detail\": \"2 image briefs planned\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"agent\": \"director\", \"phase\": \"started\", \"detail\": \"Reviewing 2 pairs on brand, diversity, execution\"}, {\"data\": {\"notes\": \"The copy needs work on two fronts. First, the voice is too clinical and lacks the brand\'s mandated warmth, humor, and natural Manglish/BM code-switching. Both variants read like generic marketing copy rather than a \'knowledgeable older sister.\' Second, the variants fail the DIVERSITY test — both are essentially the same idea (problem → solution → gift) with only superficial word changes. The \'hook\' vs \'setting\' axes aren\'t meaningfully differentiated; both could stand in for each other. Rewrite both variants with distinct angles: Variant 1 should lean into the \'hook\' axis with a more provocative, conversational opening (e.g., \'Raya gift for your kulit berminyak bestie?\'). Variant 2 should genuinely shift to the \'setting\' axis by focusing on the office environment and colleague dynamic, not just mentioning a drawer. Use natural code-switching (1-2 instances max), shorter sentences, and the brand\'s plainspoken tone. Avoid clinical phrasing like \'complete set\' or \'no need to add anything\' — make it sound like advice from a friend.\", \"verdict\": \"revise_copy\"}, \"agent\": \"director\", \"phase\": \"failed\", \"detail\": \"Verdict: revise_copy — The copy needs work on two fronts. First, the voice is too clinical and lacks the brand\'s mandated warmth, humor, and natural Manglish/BM code-switching. Both variants read like generic marketing copy rather than a \'knowledgeable older sister.\' Second, the variants fail the DIVERSITY test — both are essentially the same idea (problem → solution → gift) with only superficial word changes. The \'hook\' vs \'setting\' axes aren\'t meaningfully differentiated; both could stand in for each other. Rewrite both variants with distinct angles: Variant 1 should lean into the \'hook\' axis with a more provocative, conversational opening (e.g., \'Raya gift for your kulit berminyak bestie?\'). Variant 2 should genuinely shift to the \'setting\' axis by focusing on the office environment and colleague dynamic, not just mentioning a drawer. Use natural code-switching (1-2 instances max), shorter sentences, and the brand\'s plainspoken tone. Avoid clinical phrasing like \'complete set\' or \'no need to add anything\' — make it sound like advice from a friend.\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"agent\": \"system\", \"phase\": \"failed\", \"detail\": \"Revision budget spent after 2 passes — handing the work over flagged\"}, {\"data\": {\"passed\": false, \"revisions\": 2}, \"agent\": \"system\", \"phase\": \"failed\", \"detail\": \"2 variants after 2 revisions — flagged for you\"}, {\"data\": {\"axes\": [\"cast\", \"proof\"], \"concept_id\": \"11\"}, \"agent\": \"system\", \"phase\": \"started\", \"detail\": \"Crew opened on “Office Raya prep — surviving the pre-Raya rush with a skincare refresh, positioned as a \'Raya promotion terbaik\' for the KL office worker.”\"}, {\"data\": {\"chunks\": [\"brand.md#0-76302cee87b2c58a\", \"products.md#2-1fd832e6cfacf871\", \"products.md#0-9acf1c4f15ecbab2\", \"products.md#3-09de9fb1f5dd796b\", \"products.md#1-ff70df38bba8b661\", \"campaigns.md#2-7dbaaede50334936\", \"brand.md#1-9eae976fa1da0c9c\", \"brand.md#2-0304363243e2d334\"]}, \"agent\": \"system\", \"phase\": \"finished\", \"detail\": \"Retrieved 8 brand chunks as ground truth\"}, {\"data\": {\"axes\": [\"cast\", \"proof\"], \"revising\": false}, \"agent\": \"copywriter\", \"phase\": \"started\", \"detail\": \"Writing 2 variants, one per axis\"}, {\"data\": {\"headlines\": [\"Kakak in the next cubicle\", \"8 out of 10 said less greasy\"]}, \"agent\": \"copywriter\", \"phase\": \"finished\", \"detail\": \"2 variants written\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"agent\": \"visual_planner\", \"phase\": \"started\", \"detail\": \"Planning 2 images around the finished copy\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"agent\": \"visual_planner\", \"phase\": \"finished\", \"detail\": \"2 image briefs planned\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"agent\": \"director\", \"phase\": \"started\", \"detail\": \"Reviewing 2 pairs on brand, diversity, execution\"}, {\"data\": {\"notes\": \"Variant 1 (cast) has the right voice but the headline \'Kakak in the next cubicle\' is not a clear benefit or hook — it\'s a character description. Rewrite the headline to tie the kakak to a concrete skin outcome (e.g. \'Why the kakak in the next cubicle still looks fresh at 5pm\'). Body copy is mostly on-brand and humidity/32°C claim is supported, but \'so your kulit berminyak finally calms down\' overreaches — the supported claim is about feeling less greasy (serum test panel), not that the product \'calms\' oily skin. Change to \'so your kulit berminyak feels less greasy\'. Variant 2 (proof) is strong on the supported claim (\'8 in 10 of our 120-person Malaysian test panel said skin felt less greasy by week 4\') but the body adds two unsupported product facts: \'absorbs in 30 seconds\' and \'memang okay under your sunscreen\' — these are true for the hero serum, not for the brand as a whole, and this variant\'s proof angle is about the serum\'s test panel, so either anchor the variant explicitly to the serum or drop those two lines. Also \'Lightweight, absorbs in 30 seconds\' is a comma splice; break into two short sentences per brand rhythm. The two variants do differ meaningfully on the assigned axes (cast = character-led narrative vs proof = panel-stat-led), so diversity passes. Fix the copy above, then visuals can be replanned around the tightened headlines.\", \"verdict\": \"revise_copy\"}, \"agent\": \"director\", \"phase\": \"failed\", \"detail\": \"Verdict: revise_copy — Variant 1 (cast) has the right voice but the headline \'Kakak in the next cubicle\' is not a clear benefit or hook — it\'s a character description. Rewrite the headline to tie the kakak to a concrete skin outcome (e.g. \'Why the kakak in the next cubicle still looks fresh at 5pm\'). Body copy is mostly on-brand and humidity/32°C claim is supported, but \'so your kulit berminyak finally calms down\' overreaches — the supported claim is about feeling less greasy (serum test panel), not that the product \'calms\' oily skin. Change to \'so your kulit berminyak feels less greasy\'. Variant 2 (proof) is strong on the supported claim (\'8 in 10 of our 120-person Malaysian test panel said skin felt less greasy by week 4\') but the body adds two unsupported product facts: \'absorbs in 30 seconds\' and \'memang okay under your sunscreen\' — these are true for the hero serum, not for the brand as a whole, and this variant\'s proof angle is about the serum\'s test panel, so either anchor the variant explicitly to the serum or drop those two lines. Also \'Lightweight, absorbs in 30 seconds\' is a comma splice; break into two short sentences per brand rhythm. The two variants do differ meaningfully on the assigned axes (cast = character-led narrative vs proof = panel-stat-led), so diversity passes. Fix the copy above, then visuals can be replanned around the tightened headlines.\"}, {\"data\": {\"target\": \"copywriter\", \"revision\": 1}, \"agent\": \"system\", \"phase\": \"started\", \"detail\": \"Revision 1 of 2 → copywriter\"}, {\"data\": {\"axes\": [\"cast\", \"proof\"], \"revising\": true}, \"agent\": \"copywriter\", \"phase\": \"started\", \"detail\": \"Rewriting 2 variants, one per axis\"}, {\"data\": {\"headlines\": [\"Why the kakak in the next cubicle still looks fresh at 5pm\", \"8 in 10 said less greasy by week 4\"]}, \"agent\": \"copywriter\", \"phase\": \"finished\", \"detail\": \"2 variants written\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"agent\": \"visual_planner\", \"phase\": \"started\", \"detail\": \"Planning 2 images around the finished copy\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"agent\": \"visual_planner\", \"phase\": \"finished\", \"detail\": \"2 image briefs planned\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"agent\": \"director\", \"phase\": \"started\", \"detail\": \"Reviewing 2 pairs on brand, diversity, execution\"}, {\"data\": {\"notes\": \"Copy passes all three tests — voice is warm and plainspoken with natural code-switching (\'kulit berminyak\'), claims match company knowledge (humidity context, 8-in-10 panel stat, 30-second absorption for the hydrating serum), and the two variants genuinely differ: Variant 1 uses a relatable character (\'kakak in the next cubicle\') on the cast axis, while Variant 2 leads with the clinical proof stat on the proof axis. They are not reworded versions of the same idea.\\n\\nVisual problems only:\\n\\n**Variant 1 (cast):** The image prompt describes the subject positioned mid-left with the right two-thirds as soft bokeh, but the text placement puts headline and body in the top-right and CTA in the bottom-right — this stacks all text on the blurred wall area where contrast will be weak and readability poor. Move the subject to the right third (portrait on right, negative space on left) so the headline and body sit on the clean pale wall, and keep the CTA bottom-left over the desk surface gradient. Also, \'golden-hour sunlight streaming through horizontal blinds casting stripes across her cheek\' will create harsh lines on the face that undercut the \'fresh, composed\' mood — change to soft, diffused window light without stripe patterns.\\n\\n**Variant 2 (proof):** The prompt asks for a \'niacinamide molecular diagram subtly embossed into the surface\' — image generators cannot reliably produce legible molecular diagrams and this will render as visual noise that clashes with the clean, trustworthy mood. Remove the molecular diagram entirely. Also, the prompt places the serum bottle in the lower-right but text placement puts the CTA in the bottom-left \'just above the serum bottle\' — this is contradictory. Either move the bottle to the bottom-left and keep text bottom-right, or keep the bottle bottom-right and place the CTA bottom-left away from it (not \'just above\' it). Recommend: bottle lower-right, headline and body top-left, CTA bottom-left with clear separation from the bottle.\", \"verdict\": \"revise_visuals\"}, \"agent\": \"director\", \"phase\": \"failed\", \"detail\": \"Verdict: revise_visuals — Copy passes all three tests — voice is warm and plainspoken with natural code-switching (\'kulit berminyak\'), claims match company knowledge (humidity context, 8-in-10 panel stat, 30-second absorption for the hydrating serum), and the two variants genuinely differ: Variant 1 uses a relatable character (\'kakak in the next cubicle\') on the cast axis, while Variant 2 leads with the clinical proof stat on the proof axis. They are not reworded versions of the same idea.\\n\\nVisual problems only:\\n\\n**Variant 1 (cast):** The image prompt describes the subject positioned mid-left with the right two-thirds as soft bokeh, but the text placement puts headline and body in the top-right and CTA in the bottom-right — this stacks all text on the blurred wall area where contrast will be weak and readability poor. Move the subject to the right third (portrait on right, negative space on left) so the headline and body sit on the clean pale wall, and keep the CTA bottom-left over the desk surface gradient. Also, \'golden-hour sunlight streaming through horizontal blinds casting stripes across her cheek\' will create harsh lines on the face that undercut the \'fresh, composed\' mood — change to soft, diffused window light without stripe patterns.\\n\\n**Variant 2 (proof):** The prompt asks for a \'niacinamide molecular diagram subtly embossed into the surface\' — image generators cannot reliably produce legible molecular diagrams and this will render as visual noise that clashes with the clean, trustworthy mood. Remove the molecular diagram entirely. Also, the prompt places the serum bottle in the lower-right but text placement puts the CTA in the bottom-left \'just above the serum bottle\' — this is contradictory. Either move the bottle to the bottom-left and keep text bottom-right, or keep the bottle bottom-right and place the CTA bottom-left away from it (not \'just above\' it). Recommend: bottle lower-right, headline and body top-left, CTA bottom-left with clear separation from the bottle.\"}, {\"data\": {\"target\": \"visual_planner\", \"revision\": 2}, \"agent\": \"system\", \"phase\": \"started\", \"detail\": \"Revision 2 of 2 → visual_planner\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"agent\": \"visual_planner\", \"phase\": \"started\", \"detail\": \"Planning 2 images around the finished copy\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"agent\": \"visual_planner\", \"phase\": \"finished\", \"detail\": \"2 image briefs planned\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"agent\": \"director\", \"phase\": \"started\", \"detail\": \"Reviewing 2 pairs on brand, diversity, execution\"}, {\"data\": {\"notes\": \"\", \"verdict\": \"pass\"}, \"agent\": \"director\", \"phase\": \"finished\", \"detail\": \"Verdict: pass\"}, {\"data\": {\"passed\": true, \"revisions\": 2}, \"agent\": \"system\", \"phase\": \"finished\", \"detail\": \"2 variants after 2 revisions — passed\"}]',NULL,2,4,2,2,'qwen','2026-08-26 06:27:49','2026-08-26 06:27:49'),(14,9,'E2E image 4','generate','succeeded','2026-08-26 06:18:49',869663,'4 variants across 2 concepts — 2 flagged for you','[{\"data\": {\"axes\": [\"hook\", \"setting\"], \"concept_id\": \"10\"}, \"agent\": \"system\", \"phase\": \"started\", \"detail\": \"Crew opened on “Raya gift-giving made easy for the office crowd — the Kulit Sihat starter as a thoughtful, no-fuss Raya hamper.”\"}, {\"data\": {\"chunks\": [\"products.md#4-b9423d548dbcfac4\", \"brand.md#1-9eae976fa1da0c9c\", \"campaigns.md#3-b2c3e00cda085e89\", \"products.md#2-1fd832e6cfacf871\", \"products.md#0-9acf1c4f15ecbab2\", \"brand.md#2-0304363243e2d334\", \"campaigns.md#2-7dbaaede50334936\", \"brand.md#3-b27c3b7212dcf820\"]}, \"agent\": \"system\", \"phase\": \"finished\", \"detail\": \"Retrieved 8 brand chunks as ground truth\"}, {\"data\": {\"axes\": [\"hook\", \"setting\"], \"revising\": false}, \"agent\": \"copywriter\", \"phase\": \"started\", \"detail\": \"Writing 2 variants, one per axis\"}, {\"data\": {\"headlines\": [\"Gift that glows, not greases\", \"From desk to duit raya\"]}, \"agent\": \"copywriter\", \"phase\": \"finished\", \"detail\": \"2 variants written\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"agent\": \"visual_planner\", \"phase\": \"started\", \"detail\": \"Planning 2 images around the finished copy\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"agent\": \"visual_planner\", \"phase\": \"finished\", \"detail\": \"2 image briefs planned\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"agent\": \"director\", \"phase\": \"started\", \"detail\": \"Reviewing 2 pairs on brand, diversity, execution\"}, {\"data\": {\"notes\": \"\", \"verdict\": \"pass\"}, \"agent\": \"director\", \"phase\": \"finished\", \"detail\": \"Verdict: pass\"}, {\"data\": {\"passed\": true, \"revisions\": 0}, \"agent\": \"system\", \"phase\": \"finished\", \"detail\": \"2 variants after 0 revisions — passed\"}, {\"data\": {\"axes\": [\"cast\", \"proof\"], \