ecific character-driven narrative, and Variant 2 should lean into the test panel proof with the full approved claim and a proof-first structure.\"}, {\"data\": {\"target\": \"copywriter\", \"revision\": 1}, \"agent\": \"system\", \"phase\": \"started\", \"detail\": \"Revision 1 of 2 → copywriter\"}, {\"data\": {\"axes\": [\"cast\", \"proof\"], \"revising\": true}, \"agent\": \"copywriter\", \"phase\": \"started\", \"detail\": \"Rewriting 2 variants, one per axis\"}, {\"data\": {\"headlines\": [\"Raya Prep From the 8th Floor\", \"120 People. 4 Weeks. Real Results.\"]}, \"agent\": \"copywriter\", \"phase\": \"finished\", \"detail\": \"2 variants written\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"agent\": \"visual_planner\", \"phase\": \"started\", \"detail\": \"Planning 2 images around the finished copy\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"agent\": \"visual_planner\", \"phase\": \"finished\", \"detail\": \"2 image briefs planned\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"agent\": \"director\", \"phase\": \"started\", \"detail\": \"Reviewing 2 pairs on brand, diversity, execution\"}, {\"data\": {\"notes\": \"Variant 1 (cast axis) is fine. Variant 2 (proof axis) fails the BRAND test: it claims \\\"niacinamide 4% + polyglutamic acid that actually works under our weather\\\" — the company knowledge only supports the specific claim \\\"8 in 10 of our 120-person Malaysian test panel said skin felt less greasy by week 4,\\\" not a blanket efficacy claim about the ingredients. The copywriter must rewrite Variant 2\'s body to stick to the approved panel result and remove the unsupported ingredient-efficacy claim. The two variants do differ meaningfully along their assigned axes (personal story vs. panel proof), so DIVERSITY passes. Visuals are fine and can stay once the copy is corrected.\", \"verdict\": \"revise_copy\"}, \"agent\": \"director\", \"phase\": \"failed\", \"detail\": \"Verdict: revise_copy — Variant 1 (cast axis) is fine. Variant 2 (proof axis) fails the BRAND test: it claims \\\"niacinamide 4% + polyglutamic acid that actually works under our weather\\\" — the company knowledge only supports the specific claim \\\"8 in 10 of our 120-person Malaysian test panel said skin felt less greasy by week 4,\\\" not a blanket efficacy claim about the ingredients. The copywriter must rewrite Variant 2\'s body to stick to the approved panel result and remove the unsupported ingredient-efficacy claim. The two variants do differ meaningfully along their assigned axes (personal story vs. panel proof), so DIVERSITY passes. Visuals are fine and can stay once the copy is corrected.\"}, {\"data\": {\"target\": \"copywriter\", \"revision\": 2}, \"agent\": \"system\", \"phase\": \"started\", \"detail\": \"Revision 2 of 2 → copywriter\"}, {\"data\": {\"axes\": [\"cast\", \"proof\"], \"revising\": true}, \"agent\": \"copywriter\", \"phase\": \"started\", \"detail\": \"Rewriting 2 variants, one per axis\"}, {\"data\": {\"headlines\": [\"Raya prep, tapi kulit tak nak cooperate.\", \"120 Malaysians tried it. Here\'s what happened.\"]}, \"agent\": \"copywriter\", \"phase\": \"finished\", \"detail\": \"2 variants written\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"agent\": \"visual_planner\", \"phase\": \"started\", \"detail\": \"Planning 2 images around the finished copy\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"agent\": \"visual_planner\", \"phase\": \"finished\", \"detail\": \"2 image briefs planned\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"agent\": \"director\", \"phase\": \"started\", \"detail\": \"Reviewing 2 pairs on brand, diversity, execution\"}, {\"data\": {\"notes\": \"Variant 1 (cast): The copy is fine, but the assigned axis is \'cast\' and there is only one variant. We cannot judge diversity with only one data point. Variant 2 (proof): The copy is strong and the proof claim is supported by company knowledge. However, the body copy says \'Join the Raya promotion terbaik\' which is slightly awkward phrasing. More importantly, we need a third variant to properly assess the \'cast\' axis variation. Please provide a second \'cast\' variant with a distinctly differen