sory/audio mood assigned.\"}, {\"data\": {\"target\": \"copywriter\", \"revision\": 1}, \"agent\": \"system\", \"phase\": \"started\", \"detail\": \"Revision 1 of 2 → copywriter\"}, {\"data\": {\"axes\": [\"Setting: Morning Light Bedroom Ritual vs. Evening Vanity Prep\", \"Audio Vibe: Lo-fi Beats vs. Ambient ASMR Sounds\"], \"revising\": true}, \"agent\": \"copywriter\", \"phase\": \"started\", \"detail\": \"Rewriting 2 variants, one per axis\"}, {\"data\": {\"headlines\": [\"Morning Light, Manicure Ready.\", \"The Rhythm of Self-Care.\"]}, \"agent\": \"copywriter\", \"phase\": \"finished\", \"detail\": \"2 variants written\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"agent\": \"visual_planner\", \"phase\": \"started\", \"detail\": \"Planning 2 images around the finished copy\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"agent\": \"visual_planner\", \"phase\": \"finished\", \"detail\": \"2 image briefs planned\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"agent\": \"director\", \"phase\": \"started\", \"detail\": \"Reviewing 2 pairs on brand, diversity, execution\"}, {\"data\": {\"notes\": \"The set fails the DIVERSITY test. The variants do not differ along the assigned axes; instead, they are two completely different concepts that ignore the cross-product matrix.\\n\\n1. Axis Mismatch: The brief promises a 2x2 matrix (Setting x Audio). However, Variant 1 only addresses \'Setting: Morning\' and ignores the Audio axis. Variant 2 only addresses \'Audio: ASMR/Rhythm\' and ignores the Setting axis (though the visual is evening, the copy doesn\'t leverage the setting/axis distinction clearly against V1). There are no variants for \'Evening/Lo-fi\' or \'Morning/ASMR\'.\\n2. Lack of Differentiation: Because they tackle different axes entirely, they don\'t function as A/B tests of a single variable. They are just two different ads. To pass, you need four variants that systematically vary the two axes, or at least two variants that hold one axis constant while varying the other. Currently, V1 is \'Morning\' and V2 is \'Evening/ASMR\', making it im