ing settings WHILE holding audio constant, OR contrast Lo-fi vs ASMR audio WHILE holding setting constant. Currently, the copywriters have written two unrelated ads rather than a structured test.\"}, {\"data\": {\"target\": \"copywriter\", \"revision\": 2}, \"agent\": \"system\", \"phase\": \"started\", \"detail\": \"Revision 2 of 2 → copywriter\"}, {\"data\": {\"axes\": [\"Setting: Morning Light Bedroom Ritual vs. Evening Vanity Prep\", \"Audio Vibe: Lo-fi Beats vs. Ambient ASMR Sounds\"], \"revising\": true}, \"agent\": \"copywriter\", \"phase\": \"started\", \"detail\": \"Rewriting 2 variants, one per axis\"}, {\"data\": {\"headlines\": [\"Morning Light, Manicured.\", \"Evening Prep, Polished.\"]}, \"agent\": \"copywriter\", \"phase\": \"finished\", \"detail\": \"2 variants written\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"agent\": \"visual_planner\", \"phase\": \"started\", \"detail\": \"Planning 2 images around the finished copy\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"agent\": \"visual_planner\", \"phase\": \"finished\", \"detail\": \"2 image briefs planned\"}, {\"data\": {}, \"agent\": \"director\", \"phase\": \"started\", \"detail\": \"Reviewing 2 pairs on brand, diversity, execution\"}, {\"data\": {\"notes\": \"Variant 1 fails the BRAND test. The body copy claims the kit is for \'easy personal styling,\' which contradicts the Company Knowledge defining the product as a \'disposable self-service manicure mannequin kit\' used for \'application.\' The mannequin is a practice tool/companion for applying press-ons, not a styling tool itself. This is a functional misrepresentation. Additionally, the phrase \'manicure mannequin kit\' in Variant 1 is clunky and lacks the \'luxury beauty stylist\' voice required; it should be referred to as the \'NailIt Mannequin Kit\' or \'application companion\' as per the brand profile. Variant 2 is acceptable, but since Variant 1 requires a rewrite of the core value proposition, the whole set must be revised to ensure consistent voice and accuracy.\", \"verdict\": \"re