uring platform mega-sales\' — if this isn\'t a mega-sale window, the CTA contradicts product strategy.\n\n• **Variant 3** — \'Watch the Demo\' CTA implies a video, but the format is listed as \'video\' for the whole set, so this is redundant. The body copy also breaks the brand voice rule: it reads like a generic social caption, not the warm, plainspoken older-sister voice. No Manglish or BM code-switch, no question, no \'you\'.\n\n• **All three variants** — none of the copy uses any bilingual code-switching, which the brand voice guidelines say is \'by default\'. At least one or two variants should include a natural Manglish/BM phrase.\n\nFix: Re-assign genuinely different axes (e.g., message angle, proof type, or audience segment) OR keep the same message and vary only the visual aesthetic treatment. Rewrite the copy to match the brand voice (short sentences, questions, \'you\', one code-switch per caption). Remove the bundle push unless it\'s a mega-sale window. Make sure each variant\'s CTA matches the actual format.',2,'2026-08-26 09:15:22','2026-08-26 09:15:22'),(29,17,'aesthetic treatment','One routine. Four steps.','Why guess when you can have the full set? The Full Routine bundle gives you everything you need for humidity-proof skin, morning to night.','Get the Full Routine','{\"image_prompt\": \"An overhead-angle lifestyle shot of a Malay Malaysian woman in her early thirties sitting at a matte soft-sand table in a bright, naturally lit Kuala Lumpur apartment. She wears a relaxed linen shirt and holds the four-bottle Full Routine bundle — cleanser, serum, barrier gel-cream, and sunscreen in dew-green (#2F6B57) matte packaging — loosely in both hands, looking down at them with a small, satisfied smile. Her skin is real and textured, with a healthy humidity sheen, no filter. The table surface is uncluttered except for the four bottles. Behind her, a plain off-white wall fills the upper-right of the frame with empty negative space. Light comes from a large wi