verclaim — the company knowledge defines \'Full routine\' as the RM249 four-product bundle, so \'Full Routine Starter\' conflates two named offers; rewrite to \'RM99 for the Kulit Sihat starter?\' or \'RM99 for a full starter routine?\' to stay accurate. Variant 3 body copy says \'keeps your routine simple and effective\' — \'effective\' is an efficacy claim the guardrails don\'t support; replace with a plainspoken benefit like \'keeps your skin calm and glowing\' (glowing is allowed per the Raya campaign precedent). On diversity: all three variants are assigned the same axis \'aesthetic treatment\' and the briefs do differentiate visually (humidity bead / price card / mamak night), but the copy hooks (humidity / price / lepak late) are actually three different axes (benefit, price, lifestyle), so the axis label is wrong and the set is not truly a single-axis aesthetic variation — relabel the axis or reassign variants so they genuinely vary only aesthetic treatment while keeping one hook.',2,'2026-08-26 09:25:59','2026-08-26 09:25:59'),(36,16,'aesthetic treatment','Lepak Late, Skin Still Okay','Mamak sessions, night markets, last-minute Raya visits — your skin goes through it. The Kulit Sihat starter keeps your routine simple and effective, even when you\'re not. RM99 for the Private Sale, because you deserve skin that keeps up.','Unlock the Private Sale','{\"image_prompt\": \"A Malaysian woman in her late twenties, Malay, wearing a loose cotton tudung in soft sand, sitting at a matte dark-wood mamak-style table at night. Warm tungsten overhead light mixes with a soft cool fill from a phone screen in front of her — the signature \'mamak at 11pm\' look from the brand\'s best-performing campaign. Her skin has visible texture: a slight sheen on her T-zone, no retouching, no airbrushing. Her expression is a tired-but-happy half-smile, looking slightly off-camera like she\'s just been caught by a friend. In the lower-right of the frame, on the same matte dark table, the 