\": \"The eye enters at the mid-right where the serum bottle sits on a matte sand surface, then travels left along the clean negative space of the soft-sand backdrop. The headline and CTA live in the left two-thirds of the frame, which is deliberately empty and untextured so type set in Söhne lands with clinical clarity. A single dew-green accent stripe runs vertically at the far left edge, giving the text block a quiet anchor without competing for attention.\"}','flagged','Variant 1 fails the BRAND test. The voice is clinical and technical (\"bind to sebum, not water\", \"climate-calibrated\", \"dermatologist-reviewed\") which directly contradicts the brand voice guideline: \"never clinical, never breathless\" and \"write the way a knowledgeable older sister explains things\". The headline \"The Science of the Deal\" also misaligns with the warm, plainspoken tone. Fix: rewrite Variant 1 in the brand\'s conversational voice — explain the humidity-first benefit in plain language without jargon, and keep the clinical claims (dermatologist-reviewed, etc.) only if they can be stated naturally. Variants 2 and 3 are strong and on-voice, but the set needs all three variants to pass the brand test before shipping.',2,'2026-08-26 09:25:59','2026-08-26 09:25:59'),(38,17,'aesthetic treatment','Smart girls don\'t overpay for skincare.','You already know you need a humidity-first routine — now jom grab it at a price that actually makes sense. Kulit Sihat starter, RM99, while the deal lasts.','Add to cart before it\'s gone.','{\"image_prompt\": \"A young Malaysian Chinese woman in her mid-200s, natural skin texture visible, no heavy makeup, wearing a simple white ribbed tank top, sits against a plain soft-sand (#EDE3D3) matte wall. She is turned three-quarters toward camera, looking slightly downward and to the left with a relaxed, knowing half-smile — the expression of someone sharing a smart tip with a friend. Bright, natural daylight from a large window to her right creates so