ut the set needs all three variants to pass the brand test before shipping.',2,'2026-08-26 09:25:59','2026-08-26 09:25:59'),(39,17,'aesthetic treatment','I overpaid for my last serum.','Broke out anyway. This RM99 starter is the first routine that actually survived a KL night out — and I\'m not gatekeeping the price. Kulit berminyak? Memang okay.','Grab yours on Shopee.','{\"image_prompt\": \"A young Malaysian Malay woman in her late 20s, shot on a phone camera aesthetic — slight grain, natural auto-exposure, no studio lighting. She is in a dimly lit but warm mamak stall at night, sitting across a plastic table from the viewer. Visible skin texture, a few small blemishes on her forehead and cheek, no makeup. She looks directly into the lens with a candid, slightly tired but genuine expression, one hand resting near her jaw. Behind her, the out-of-focus bokeh shows warm yellow mamak lights and the blurred silhouette of another patron. She wears a simple oversized tee. The upper-left quadrant of the frame is empty dark wall, and the lower half of the frame — her chest and the table edge — is plain and uncluttered. Mood: intimate, unpolished, confessional, real.\", \"placement_zone\": \"bottom-center\", \"text_placement\": \"Headline \'I overpaid for my last serum.\' set in Söhne Bold off-white (#EDE3D3) sits left-aligned in the upper-left, starting about 10% from the top and 5% from the left edge, placed against the dark empty wall. Body copy in Söhne Regular off-white sits below it, same alignment, with natural Manglish phrasing preserved exactly. CTA \'Grab yours on Shopee.\' sits in a dew-green (#2F6B57) pill button, left-aligned, at the bottom-center of the frame, roughly 80% down.\", \"composition_notes\": \"The eye enters immediately at the model\'s face in the upper-center, drawn by direct eye contact and the intimate framing. The headline sits in the upper-left, overlapping the empty wall space just beside her head, so it reads as a first-person caption. The lower half of the frame — her chest, hands, and the plain wall below — is deliberately uncluttered so the body copy and CTA have a calm, untextured bed to sit on, mimicking the feel of a phone-shot story update.\"}','flagged','Variant 1 fails the BRAND test. The voice is clinical and technical (\"bind to sebum, not water\", \"climate-calibrated\", \"dermatologist-reviewed\") which directly contradicts the brand voice guideline: \"never clinical, never breathless\" and \"write the way a knowledgeable older sister explains things\". The headline \"The Science of the Deal\" also misaligns with the warm, plainspoken tone. Fix: rewrite Variant 1 in the brand\'s conversational voice — explain the humidity-first benefit in plain language without jargon, and keep the clinical claims (dermatologist-reviewed, etc.) only if they can be stated naturally. Variants 2 and 3 are strong and on-voice, but the set needs all three variants to pass the brand test before shipping.',2,'2026-08-26 09:25:59','2026-08-26 09:25:59'),(40,18,'aesthetic treatment','Golden hour, but make it matte.','Embun sunscreen blends in invisible — no white cast, no greasy shine, even when the sun hits just right. Your skin stays smooth and balanced, from the first golden glow to the last.','Shop Embun now','{\"image_prompt\": \"A young Malay woman in her mid-20s stands beside a weathered sandstone wall in a quiet Kuala Lumpur backstreet during golden hour. Warm, directional sunlight rakes across her face from the left, revealing natural skin texture — visible pores, a faint tan line, no retouching. She wears a simple cream linen shirt; her expression is calm, eyes slightly squinted against the low sun. The wall behind her is a soft, matte #EDE3D3 sand tone, completely free of text or logos. Lighting is bright but diffused by the late-afternoon haze, casting long, gentle shadows. The composition leaves the entire left half of the frame open and uncluttered, with no subject or focal detail intruding into that space. Mood is warm, grounded, and quietly confident — the \'golden hour, but make it matte\' feeling.\", \"placement_zone\": \"top-left\", \"text_placement\": \"Headline \'Golden hour, but make it matte.\' sits in the upper-left quadrant, above the body copy \'Embun sunscreen blends in invisible — no white cast, no greasy shine, even when the sun hits just right. Your skin stays smooth and balanced, from the first golden glow to the last.\' The CTA \'Shop Embun now\' is anchored at the bottom-left corner.\", \"composition_notes\": \"Eye lands first on the model\'s face in the upper-right third; the warm, uncluttered sand-colored wall to the left gives the headline a calm resting place. Visible skin texture and natural Malay features keep the image authentic to brand identity, while the matte product surface echoes the \'no shine\' promise. Golden-hour light wraps the scene without blowing out highlights, preserving the soft, editorial warmth the copy describes.\"}','flagged','Variant 3 fails the BRAND test. The headline \'Dreamy haze, zero white cast\' and body copy \'That soft-focus golden hour look? Embun makes it real\' chase the \'glass skin\' aesthetic the company knowledge explicitly says has not worked (\'Borrowing the aesthetic wholesale reads as inauthentic\'). The visual brief also describes a \'soft-focus, dreamy glow\' which contradicts the brand\'s visual identity of \'bright, natural daylight, visible skin texture\' and the voice guardrail against \'retouched skin texture\'. The copy also lacks the required bilingual code-switching (no Manglish or Bahasa Melayu) and doesn\'t reflect the \'humidity-first\' positioning that is the brand\'s competitive claim. Variants 1 and 2 are stronger but all three variants need rewrite to: (1) avoid glass-skin/dreamy aesthetic language, (2) incorporate natural code-switching, (3) emphasize humidity-first formulation, and (4) maintain plainspoken \'older sister\' voice. Once copy is revised, visuals will need replanning to match.',2,'2026-08-26 09:25:59','2026-08-26 09:25:59'),(41,18,'aesthetic treatment','Sharp light. Soft skin.','High-contrast sun calls for a sunscreen that disappears. Embun gives you invisible, humidity-proof protection — so you look glowing, not glossy, even in the harshest light.','Get yours today','{\"image_prompt\": \"A young Indian Malaysian woman in her late 20s is photographed in a tight, editorial close-up against a deep, matte off-black (#1B1B18) background. Harsh, directional sunlight enters from the right, carving a sharp line of bright highlight across the right side of her face while the left side falls into a clean, deep shadow. Her skin shows real texture — visible pores, a small freckle, no retouching — and her expression is direct and calm, looking slightly off-camera. She wears a simple white crew-neck tee that fades into the dark background. The entire left third of the frame is pure, uncluttered shadow with no subject detail, providing a stark, high-contrast canvas for text. Lighting is bright and hard on the lit side, with no fill, creating a moody, high-fashion editorial feel. Mood is sharp, confident, and modern.\", \"placement_zone\": \"top-left\", \"text_placement\": \"Headline \'Sharp light. Soft skin.\' is placed in the upper-left quadrant, over the deep shadow. Body copy \'High-contrast sun calls for a sunscreen that disappears. Embun gives you invisible, humidity-proof protection — so you look glowing, not glossy, even in the harshest light.\' sits below it in the same left-column space. The CTA \'Get yours today\' is anchored at the bottom-left corner.\", \"composition_notes\": \"The eye is drawn first to the model\'s face and the dramatic shadow play across her features in the center-right of the frame. The deep, cool shadow on the left side of the image creates a high-contrast negative space that is completely free of facial features or distracting detail — the perfect anchor for the headline. The Indian model\'s visible skin texture and natural features honor the brand\'s diversity mandate, while the off-black background keeps the mood editorial and sharp, never glossy.\"}','flagged','Variant 3 fails the BRAND test. The headline \'Dreamy haze, zero white cast\' and body copy \'That soft-focus golden hour look? Embun makes it real\' chase the \'glass skin\' aesthetic the company knowledge explicitly says has not worked (\'Borrowing the aesthetic wholesale reads as inauthentic\'). The visual brief also describes a \'soft-focus, dreamy glow\' which contradicts the brand\'s visual identity of \'bright, natural daylight, visible skin texture\' and the voice guardrail against \'retouched skin texture\'. The copy also lacks the required bilingual code-switching (no Manglish or Bahasa Melayu) and doesn\'t reflect the \'humidity-first\' positioning that is the brand\'s competitive claim. Variants 1 and 2 are stronger but all three variants need rewrite to: (1) avoid glass-skin/dreamy aesthetic language, (2) incorporate natural code-switching, (3) emphasize humidity-first formulation, and (4) maintain plainspoken \'older sister\' voice. Once copy is revised, visuals will need replanning to match.',2,'2026-08-26 09:25:59','2026-08-26 09:25:59'),(42,18,'aesthetic treatment','Dreamy haze, zero white cast.','That soft-focus golden hour look? Embun makes it real. Our lightweight, humidity-first formula melts into every skin tone, so you stay protected and naturally radiant all day.','Find your shade','{\"image_prompt\": \"A young Chinese Malaysian woman in her early 20s is photographed in a medium close-up during golden hour, standing in an open field with tall, soft grass. The light is heavily diffused by a warm, hazy late-afternoon sky, creating a soft-focus, dreamy glow across the entire scene. Her skin shows real, visible texture — no retouching — and her expression is serene, eyes closed or looking down, with a faint, natural smile. She wears a simple white top and a loosely draped scarf in dew g